The fixture of contract-test's shell checks (lean/ContractTest.lean,
shellChecks), which `mise run ffi-test` hands contract-test as its third
argument. It must stay executable (mode 100755).

- hello: prints `hello` and a line feed, and exits 0. contract-test runs it
  with `:!` over the real process service, in this directory, and expects
  the echo area to say `hello`. Shell builtins only.
